  "notes": "q = 523. With w = 2 + 1i a generator of GF(q^2)*, i^2 = -1, and chi the quadratic character of GF(q), let f(d) = chi(Im w^d) for 0 <= d <= q and X_r(k) = (-1)^k f(r + 4k) for 0 <= k < n. After sign changes of rows and columns the Paley core of order q + 1 on the points w^d is a block matrix of the four circulants X_0, X_1, X_2, X_3 and their cyclic shifts. The rows are X_0 with entry 0 set to +1 (skew), X_2 shifted by 65 (symmetric), and X_1 twice; X_3 is a shifted reversal of X_1 up to sign. This is the form A skew, B symmetric, C = D that the source proves to exist for every prime power q = 4n - 1; the rows were generated from the Paley matrix with the scripts of the n = 83 and 125 entries and not transcribed from the source. The script checked the full Paley core of order 524 and its block form entry by entry. A literature construction, not a new result; the board had no quadruple at n = 131 before."
